From: Koushick Varun <51849493+kvarun-p@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 03:01:04 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] nak: stall divergent conditional branches for 6 cycles on
 Turing

llama.cpp's bitonic argsort shaders (argsort.comp, argsort_large.comp)
intermittently produced wrong orders on a TU117: 55 of 1960 test cases
over 20 runs. Bisected with temporary switches:
  - waits on bar.sync, membar before bar.sync, and waiting on all
    scoreboards for memory ops: no fix;
  - 15-cycle stall on every instr, on control instrs, on branches, on
    conditional branches, and on conditional branches in non-uniform
    blocks: 0 failures; uniform conditional branches: no fix;
  - minimum stall on conditional branches: 4 -> 517 failures,
    5 -> 0, 6 -> 0.
All register dependencies across those branches meet the SM75 latency
tables, so this looks like a divergence timing rule. Uniform blocks are
left alone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nouveau/compiler/nak/calc_instr_deps.rs | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/calc_instr_deps.rs b/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/calc_instr_deps.rs
index c89c3357..bf437664 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/calc_instr_deps.rs
+++ b/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/calc_instr_deps.rs
@@ -1059,6 +1059,30 @@ fn calc_delays(f: &mut Function, sm: &ShaderModelInfo) -> u64 {
     min_num_static_cycles
 }
 
+/// On Turing (seen on TU117), a conditional branch that can diverge needs
+/// to stall for at least 5 cycles before the next instruction issues.
+/// With less, llama.cpp's bitonic argsort shaders intermittently produce
+/// wrong results; 4 cycles makes it worse than the default of 1.  All data
+/// dependencies around the failing branches meet the SM75 latency tables,
+/// so this is a divergence-timing rule rather than a register latency.
+/// Uniform branches are unaffected.  Use 6 for a cycle of margin.
+fn delay_divergent_branches_sm75(f: &mut Function) {
+    const MIN_DELAY: u8 = 6;
+    for b in &mut f.blocks {
+        if b.uniform {
+            continue;
+        }
+        for instr in &mut b.instrs {
+            if instr.is_branch()
+                && !instr.is_branch_always_taken()
+                && instr.deps.delay < MIN_DELAY
+            {
+                instr.deps.set_delay(MIN_DELAY);
+            }
+        }
+    }
+}
+
 impl Shader<'_> {
     pub fn assign_deps_serial(&mut self) {
         for f in &mut self.functions {
@@ -1105,6 +1129,9 @@ impl Shader<'_> {
             for f in &mut self.functions {
                 assign_barriers(f, self.sm);
                 min_num_static_cycles += calc_delays(f, self.sm);
+                if self.sm.sm() == 75 {
+                    delay_divergent_branches_sm75(f);
+                }
             }
 
             if DEBUG.cycles() {
